Lifeline is a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]] in the lower hull of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], keeping what was once a hospital on the third floor, close to the surface and north of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence/Machine God|Machine God]]'s fane. The place belongs to the domain of life.

The years have not been kind to it. The Machine God counts it a friend and calls it dying, or no longer sane in the way the Machine God kept itself sane. Its halls are the one part of the lower decks that is kept: dustless, repaired, lit by white lamps and worked by machinery that still runs, where the rest has gone dirty and dark over seven hundred years.

The hospital is the home of a sleeping clan of [[Bestiary/Ugathal|oogathals]], who came to the strider seven hundred years ago and lie there still while their keepers walk. The sleepers lie in glass vats through the halls, and a chitinous, crab-like creature keeps the place besides them, perched on a raised platform and working the hostile magic that guards the sleep. The Machine God would see them all destroyed, and says it could take Lifeline's place if the hospital were cleared, though it would not eat the corpse of a fallen friend.
